# Flow-manager browser-turn monitoring (binding)

Canonical contract: [`.claude/skills/create-issue-draft/SKILL.md`](../../.claude/skills/create-issue-draft/SKILL.md) — **Browser-GPT turn transport — Issue #1120**.

## One normal monitoring path

For create-issue-draft and pack-review Browser-GPT work, `npm run chatgpt-browser-turn -- turn ...` is the normal low-token fast path and the only routine browser-turn monitor.

- One invocation opens one dedicated owned ChatGPT tab, sends the exact user prompt once, and then observes that same tab until completion or an invocation-local failure.
- Page/DOM completion is sufficient. Do not require service-terminal/network witness fields after the final assistant reply is visibly stable and no longer generating.
- The helper may use bounded low-frequency polling after initial dispatch observation. A normal waiting/generating poll is not an incident.
- A direct helper failure affects only that invocation. It does not authorize a profile-, conversation-, task-, Issue-, PR-, or agent-wide gate.
- Owned-tab cleanup is progressive and local. Never close or commandeer sibling/foreign ChatGPT tabs.

## Legacy state is not admission authority

Do **not** gate create/review progress on any of the following:

- `status/list`, `clear`, capability/Gate-B;
- `possible_delivery`, `profile_wall`, stale recovery/orphan records;
- browser/profile/conversation mutexes, claims, queues, leases, or helper-wide blocked state;
- shell PID/log growth as evidence that ChatGPT is still generating.

Legacy control commands may remain available for compatibility/evidence lookup, but they cannot decide whether a new Browser-GPT invocation may start.

## Unexpected events and restart

When the helper directly observes foreign/interleaved user activity, page loss, UI contract failure, cleanup failure, timeout, or another unexpected browser-turn event:

1. return/report the invocation-local result;
2. append the compact event best-effort to `~/.local/state/create-issue-draft/browser-turn-recurrence.jsonl`;
3. include the same direct event in the current flow-manager report;
4. leave sibling Browser-GPT work alone.

A lost/crashed invocation may be retried as a fresh chat with a fresh send. Duplicate recoverable GPT text is an accepted residual risk; do not recreate the old recovery/clear protocol to prevent it.

## Sanctioned one-shot page probe

When direct page diagnosis is genuinely needed, use only the canonical read-only utility:

```bash
npm run browser-gpt-page-probe -- list --cdp http://127.0.0.1:9222
npm run browser-gpt-page-probe -- inspect --cdp http://127.0.0.1:9222 --target-id <exact-target-id>
```

An exact normalized ChatGPT conversation URL may replace `--target-id` for inspection only when it resolves to exactly one already-open target. The probe runs once and exits. It never navigates, sends, clicks, focuses, scrolls, reloads, creates, closes, or reorders tabs.

The probe is **diagnostic only**:

- `generation_in_progress: false` is not completion evidence;
- node counts, hashes, witnesses, and an exported node file do not authorize publication, retry, resend, cleanup, admission, recovery, review capture, or stage progression;
- use inspection output to select exactly one node representation for optional offline export; never request or construct a transcript dump;
- exported text may be sensitive. The caller supplies a new path in an existing directory and owns protection and cleanup of the resulting file.

Do not replace this command with raw CDP WebSocket scripts, Playwright snippets, `salvage-*.mjs`, caller-supplied selectors/JavaScript, a watch loop, or a second supported probe.

## Forbidden duplicate monitoring and authority

- No independent 5–10 or 10–15 minute watchdog layered over the helper.
- No periodic browser-tab sweeper that closes tabs it did not open.
- No reporting "still running" from shell/PID/log state alone.
- No probe-driven takeover, helper bypass, resend, or workflow progression.

The one-shot page probe diagnoses an already-open page; it is not a fallback state machine or browser-turn owner.

## Session handoff

Never end a flow-manager turn with only "background job running". Status must name the owned chat URL when known, the helper result or latest direct observation, any direct incident surfaced by the helper, and the next flow action.
